---
import PrepLayout from '../layouts/PrepLayout.astro';
---

<PrepLayout
  title="ML interview practice method"
  description="A closed-book practice protocol and self-scoring rubric for senior ML interviews."
  heading="Practice retrieval, not recognition."
  lede="Reading a good answer can create false confidence. This protocol turns each question into an attempt, a diagnosis, and a scheduled retry."
>
  <p class="intro">Use this method on any <a href="/questions/">question page</a>. Practice Mode provides the timer, private scratchpad, rubric, and a local self-score.</p>

  <h2>The 8-minute attempt</h2>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li><strong>Read only the prompt.</strong> Do not scan the answer headings or open references.</li>
    <li><strong>Clarify aloud.</strong> State the objective, assumptions, constraints, and what success means.</li>
    <li><strong>Give a structured answer.</strong> Lead with an outline, then fill in decisions, mechanisms, and trade-offs.</li>
    <li><strong>Handle one follow-up.</strong> Ask what an interviewer would challenge and answer it one level deeper.</li>
    <li><strong>Stop at eight minutes.</strong> A bounded attempt makes gaps visible and improves answer control.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The five-part rubric</h2>
  <div class="rubric-table">
    <section><h3>Problem framing</h3><p>Did you identify the user, objective, constraints, and cost of failure before proposing a solution?</p></section>
    <section><h3>Technical depth</h3><p>Did you explain why the mechanism works and survive a follow-up beyond the headline?</p></section>
    <section><h3>Trade-offs</h3><p>Did you compare credible alternatives and state what evidence would reverse your decision?</p></section>
    <section><h3>Evidence</h3><p>Did you use concrete metrics, experience, or realistic failure modes rather than abstractions alone?</p></section>
    <section><h3>Communication</h3><p>Was the answer easy to follow, appropriately concise, and collaborative under uncertainty?</p></section>
  </div>

  <h2>Self-score and retry</h2>
  <ul class="score-list">
    <li><strong>Weak:</strong> you missed the frame or core mechanism. Rebuild the answer and retry closed-book in two days.</li>
    <li><strong>Review:</strong> the core was sound but depth or trade-offs were thin. Retry in one week.</li>
    <li><strong>Confident:</strong> the answer was structured and follow-up ready. Check it once in the final week.</li>
  </ul>

  <section class="callout">
    <h2>Do not grade for eloquence</h2>
    <p>A polished answer with weak decisions is not strong. Grade whether the reasoning is explicit, falsifiable, and calibrated to the target level.</p>
  </section>

  <h2>A 45-minute practice block</h2>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li>Two 8-minute closed-book attempts.</li>
    <li>Five minutes of rubric review after each attempt.</li>
    <li>Ten minutes reading only the sections that address observed gaps.</li>
    <li>Five minutes rewriting the answer outline from memory.</li>
  </ol>

  <p><a href="/questions/">Choose a question and start Practice Mode →</a></p>
</PrepLayout>

<style>
  .rubric-table { display: grid; gap: .65rem; margin: 1.2rem 0; }
  .rubric-table section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: .9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--c-rule); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .rubric-table h3, .rubric-table p { margin: 0; }
  .rubric-table p { color: var(--c-text-soft); }
  .score-list { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .score-list li { margin: .65rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .rubric-table section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .25rem; } }
</style>
